    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Daily job — THE TABLE IS THE ROSTER\n\nMembership comes from course_telegram_members, not from Teachable. Only rows whose `batch` matches a row in course_telegram_batches are processed, and progress is fetched **one user at a time** via /courses/{id}/progress?user_id=. Nothing here pulls the whole enrollment list.\n\n**Order:** fetch each member progress -> update their row -> DM them if due -> after the loop, re-read the table and post the batch scoreboard. The channel numbers are therefore counted over the table, so the public number and the private ones always agree.\n\n**Column meanings:**\n- percent_complete = latest observed progress, refreshed every run for every member\n- prev_percent = progress at the LAST DM, written only when a DM is sent. delta = percent_complete - prev_percent is what the copy says.\n\n**SAFETY GATES (default-safe):** Config.dry_run=true bypasses every send; dm_active / channel_post_active per batch row; dm_enabled per member row. Progress is still fetched and rows still updated during a dry run — only sending is suppressed, so the run is fully inspectable.\n\n**There is deliberately NO test-recipient allowlist.** One existed during testing and was removed: left populated at go-live it silently drops every real student with not_in_test_allowlist while the run still reports success. To limit a test, limit the members table instead.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 960,
        "color": 5
      },
